WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
Hi everyone.

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.600
For those who don’t know me yet,
I’m Kristine Dennis,

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.040
a scientist who has
spent my career

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.600
working in public health
and nutrition research.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.080
At NutritionFacts, I serve as
Senior Research Scientist

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.440
and, alongside Dr. Greger,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.600
research and write
new video scripts.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.880
For these next couple of videos,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.640
I got to take a deep dive into the
research on raising plant-based kids.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.880
As a parent of a plant-
based kid myself

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.800
and a nutrition research nerd,
this was both fun and fascinating.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.200
I’m going to cover everything
that goes into raising kids

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.360
on well-planned
plant-based diets,

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.080
including what does
‘well-planned’ actually mean,

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.960
some potential benefits of eating
plant-based during pregnancy,

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.080
and a few special nutrients everyone
should be paying attention to

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.334
— regardless of diet.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:46.320
"Preventing Gestational Diabetes
During Pregnancy with Diet"

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.000
Over the past two decades,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.600
scientific and
professional nutrition,

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.120
and pediatric associations,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.320
have issued official statements
and published position papers

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.080
about adopting vegan diets
during crucial life stages,

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.000
including pregnancy
and lactation,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.560
infancy, and childhood.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.240
While some of these associations

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.800
firmly agree
a well-designed vegan diet

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.080
can be healthy and support
normal growth and development,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.920
others are more reserved,

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.520
and some caution against
vegan diets for children.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:16.560
Those that are supportive

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.720
include the American
Dietetic Association,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.000
which has held this position
for more than 25 years,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.760
as well as
professional associations

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.880
in Australia, Canada,
Portugal, Italy,

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.440
the UK, Finland,
Germany, and Norway,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.160
and Europe more broadly.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.640
More reserved opinions
also came out of the UK

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.040
and Europe, including Spain,

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.120
and downright
dismissive positions

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.640
have come out of Slovenia,

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.360
Germany, Italy,
France, and Belgium.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.640
What does the evidence say
about vegan diets in children?

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.120
Part of the challenge
starts at the very beginning,

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.800
with the exclusion
of pregnant people

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.760
from clinical trials in general.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.200
With such compelling needs,

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.960
why are pregnant women
largely excluded

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.200
from clinical research?

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.440
Often due to ethical concerns,

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.640
dominated by fears
of fetal harm.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.120
Even non-pregnant women
of reproductive age

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.880
often have to commit
to contraception

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.480
during the research period,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.840
and those who become pregnant

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.280
must leave the study
with their data excluded.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.920
That all adds up to a lack
of clinical trial data

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.200
on pregnant women.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.160
Paradoxically,
these precautionary measures

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.800
may not have made pregnant moms
or their babies safer

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.920
because of the resulting
lack of evidence.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.560
Some of the commentary
around vegan diets for children

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.840
includes this same concern
about the lack of data.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.360
One researcher stated,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.240
"In children we do not
have many good quality studies,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.920
and the studies we do have come
mostly from vegetarian children,

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.200
and they are of
very varying quality."

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.000
But researchers are
attempting to fill this void,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.160
starting with,
"To vegan or not to vegan

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.160
when pregnant, lactating,
or feeding young children."

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.920
The oldest
and largest association

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.840
of nutritional professionals
in the world,

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.400
the Academy
of Nutrition and Dietetics

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.400
considers a completely
plant-based diet

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.160
to be suitable during pregnancy,

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.560
lactation, infancy,
and childhood,

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.720
provided it is well-planned.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.760
What exactly
does well-planned mean?

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.920
First of all, a diet
rich in a wide variety

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.240
of plant foods;
grains, legumes

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.960
(such as beans, lentils,
split peas, and chickpeas),

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.200
fruits and veggies,
nuts and seeds,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.120
herbs and spices.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.720
We want to limit vegetable fats

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.600
so they don't displace
more nutrient-dense foods,

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.560
and if you do use them,
choosing them carefully,

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.480
for example, avoiding
trans fats and tropical oils.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.240
Also taking a DHA supplement,
consuming enough calcium,

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.040
and ensuring
sufficient vitamin D.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.480
And most importantly,

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.880
not forgetting
about vitamin B12,

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.600
as Dr. Greger
has covered extensively

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.400
because it is so important
to ensure a regular

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.400
and reliable source
of vitamin B12.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.760
Balanced plant-based diets

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.680
mean eating a wide
variety of plant foods

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.480
in order to sufficiently
meet energy requirements,

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.320
and paying attention
to some nutrients

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.760
that may be critical,
iodine included.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.160
It's one nutrient that
should also be supplemented

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.720
during pregnancy
and breastfeeding.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.360
What are the impacts
on the mother's health

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.360
of following a vegetarian diet
during pregnancy?

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.000
Gestational diabetes
affects around 14 percent

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.680
of pregnancies globally,

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.800
and even more
in some regions of the world.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.880
It's also at the center
of the vicious cycle

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.680
of diabetes begetting diabetes.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.520
Linked not only
to adverse pregnancy

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.120
and birth outcomes,

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.680
but greater long-term risk
of cardiometabolic disorders

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.760
for both moms and babies.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.240
Research suggests
beneficial impacts

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.680
of plant-based diets
on blood sugar control.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.240
What effect might that have
on risk of gestational diabetes?

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:52.160
A systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.680
on plant-based
dietary patterns

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.600
and gestational diabetes risk
found that those who ate

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.600
closer to a healthy,
plant-based diet

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:01.600
had a significantly lower risk

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.560
of developing
gestational diabetes.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.080
Evidence from the
Harvard Nurses' Health Study II

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.960
suggests these benefits extend
to hypertensive disorders,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.560
like preeclampsia,

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.320
with a 20 percent lower risk

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:17.680
among those eating
the most plant-based diets.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.000
And this lower risk
could benefit moms' health

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.440
for years to come,

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.840
as hypertensive disorders
during pregnancy

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.080
are associated with
increased risk of stroke

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.240
later in life.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.160
Note that Dr. Greger
previously covered

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.960
other pregnancy
outcomes, as well.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:34.560
Once the baby arrives,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.000
what do we know about
plant-based diets

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.400
and feeding babies
and young children?

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.072
I'll cover that next.

